04/17/2025 14:17:38 - WARNING - pvg.utils.utils - Could not find ```...```, <solution>...</solution>, or <injected_solution>...</injected_solution> block in completion text. Returning raw text. Text was:
---
The challenge here is that teleporting can shorten your walk between towns, but introduces an unbroken run from point to point. This is like being able to use your teleports on marshmallows; you can make progress more quickly but risk the inevitable crash when you go through fuel or run out of marshmallows.

We want to start at town 1 and end at town 4. To do that, we need to figure out a strategy that takes a few steps forward for each teleport and as little as possible on the final part. The game has no guarantees, but I’ll rely on the fact that, with teleporting, there’s a pattern: every 2 teleports you go three steps forward and 1 back.

When you teleport after each step forward, you can capture the least cost path by putting the cost of each step forward and step back together. Here’s what I’ve got:

<code>
def solution(N, A, B, X):
    """
    :type N: int
    :type A: int
    :type B: int
    :type X: List[int]
    :rtype: int
    """
    minCost = float('inf')

    for i in range(N - 1):
        # For each teleport except the last one
        minCost = min(minCost,
                      (i * B + A) +
                      (X[i] - X[i + 1] + 3 * A) +
                      A + (X[i] + B - X[i + 1]) -
                      (i * B + A))

    return minCost
</code>

I hope that gives you a start!
</solution>

---
